From: pmOS Q706F fixes
Subject: [PATCH] power: bq27xxx: do not report full while discharging

The Q706F gauge keeps the full-charge flag set at 100% after the
USB-C cable is removed, while current is already negative. UPower
then stays on the plugged-in full icon, so plug and unplug look
the same.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
@@ -1899,7 +1899,8 @@ static int bq27xxx_battery_current_and_status(
 		val_curr->intval = curr;
 
 	if (val_status) {
-		if (bq27xxx_battery_is_full(di, flags))
+		/* FC stays set at 100% while the pack is discharging. */
+		if (bq27xxx_battery_is_full(di, flags) && curr >= 0)
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
 		else if (curr > 0)
 			val_status->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
